{"ingredient/sweet-potato":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sweet-potato","n":"Sweet potato","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 10 dishes across 10 cuisines","intro":[["The sweet potato or sweetpotato (Ipomoea batatas) is a dicotyledonous plant in the morning glory family, Convolvulaceae. Its sizeable, starchy, sweet-tasting, tuberous roots are used as a root vegetable, which is a staple food in parts of the world. Cultivars of the sweet potato have been bred to bear tubers with flesh and skin of various colors. Moreover, the young shoots and leaves are eaten as greens with nutritional composition comparable to spinach. The sweet potato and the potato are only distantly related, both being in the order Solanales. Although darker sweet potatoes are often known as yams in parts of North America, they are even more distant from actual yams, which are monocots in the order Dioscoreales."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sweet-potato"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sweet_potato"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":10,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Kolak (food)","dish/kolak-food"],["Tinutuan","dish/tinutuan"]]],["Argentine cuisine","cuisine/argentine-cuisine",[["Dulce de batata","dish/dulce-de-batata"]]],["Gujarati cuisine","cuisine/gujarati-cuisine",[["Undhiyu","dish/undhiyu"]]],["North Korean cuisine","cuisine/north-korean-cuisine",[["Pyongyang Raengmyon","dish/pyongyang-raengmyon"]]],["Paraguayan cuisine","cuisine/paraguayan-cuisine",[["Dulce de batata","dish/dulce-de-batata"]]],["Peruvian cuisine","cuisine/peruvian-cuisine",[["Picarones","dish/picarones"]]],["South Korean cuisine","cuisine/south-korean-cuisine",[["Milmyeon","dish/milmyeon"]]],["Taiwan cuisine","cuisine/taiwan-cuisine",[["Bah-uân","dish/bah-uan"]]],["Uruguayan cuisine","cuisine/uruguayan-cuisine",[["Dulce de batata","dish/dulce-de-batata"]]],["Vietnamese cuisine","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",[["Bánh tráng","dish/banh-trang"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Sweet potatoes","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":90918896,"top":[["China","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",51391509],["Malawi","cuisine/malawian-cuisine",7489536],["Nigeria","cuisine/nigerian-cuisine",4085862],["Tanzania","cuisine/tanzanian-cuisine",2437354],["Angola","cuisine/angolan-cuisine",1906522],["Indonesia","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",1639777],["Ethiopia","cuisine/ethiopian-cuisine",1513233],["Rwanda","cuisine/rwandan-cuisine",1337551],["Madagascar","cuisine/malagasy-cuisine",1287755],["United States of America","cuisine/american-cuisine",1248990],["Uganda","cuisine/ugandan-cuisine",1244555],["India","cuisine/indian-cuisine",1208199],["Vietnam","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",1094642],["Burundi","cuisine/burundian-cuisine",1025879],["Brazil","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine",888300]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Bamboo shoot","ingredient/bamboo-shoot"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Tapioca","ingredient/tapioca"],["Banana","ingredient/banana"],["Noodle","ingredient/noodle"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Corn starch","ingredient/corn-starch"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"],["Shiitake","ingredient/shiitake"],["Anchovy","ingredient/anchovy"],["Bean curd","ingredient/bean-curd"],["Bumbu (seasoning)","ingredient/bumbu-seasoning"],["Caraway seed","ingredient/caraway-seed"]]},{"h":"Mentioned in","links":[["Amazonian Kichwa foodways","cuisine/amazonian-kichwa-foodways"],["Guaraní foodways","cuisine/guarani-foodways"],["Kānaka Maoli foodways","cuisine/kanaka-maoli-foodways"],["Maya cuisine","cuisine/maya-cuisine"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/5/58/Ipomoea_batatas_006.JPG/500px-Ipomoea_batatas_006.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Llez","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ipomoea_batatas_006.JPG"}},"dish/bobo-de-camarao":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/bobo-de-camarao","n":"Bobó de camarão","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Brazilian cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Bobó de camarão, sometimes referred to as shrimp bobó in English, is a chowder-like Brazilian dish of shrimp in a purée of manioc meal with coconut milk, herbs, ginger, red palm oil, and other ingredients."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-bobo-de-camarao"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bob%C3%B3_de_camar%C3%A3o"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Brazilian cuisine","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Manioc","ingredient/manioc"],["Shrimp","ingredient/shrimp"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olivia's Cuisine","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"oliviascuisine.com","note":"Brazilian-born Olivia Mesquita's blog, with a large section of Brazilian classics.","url":"https://oliviascuisine.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Easy and Delish","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"easyanddelish.com","note":"Brazilian recipe collection from a Brazilian-born home cook based in the US.","url":"https://www.easyanddelish.com/easy-brazilian-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Brazilian cuisine","links":[["Arabu","dish/arabu"],["Arroz carreteiro","dish/arroz-carreteiro"],["Bauru (sandwich)","dish/bauru-sandwich"],["Beijinho","dish/beijinho"],["Beirute","dish/beirute"],["Bockwurst","dish/bockwurst"],["Bolo de fubá","dish/bolo-de-fuba"],["Brigadeiro","dish/brigadeiro"],["Canja de galinha","dish/canja-de-galinha"],["Coxinha","dish/coxinha"],["Feijoada","dish/feijoada"],["Maniçoba","dish/manicoba"],["Manuê","dish/manue"],["Marmelada de Santa Luzia","dish/marmelada-de-santa-luzia"],["Pão na chapa","dish/pao-na-chapa"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Sobá","dish/soba"],["Xis (sandwich)","dish/xis-sandwich"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/7/7b/Bobo_a_Dish_from_Brazil.JPG/500px-Bobo_a_Dish_from_Brazil.JPG","w":500,"h":373,"by":"Victorgrigas","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bobo_a_Dish_from_Brazil.JPG"}},"dish/fasnacht-doughnut":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/fasnacht-doughnut","n":"Fasnacht (doughnut)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Cuisine of the Pennsylvania Dutch","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Fasnacht (also spelled fastnacht, faschnacht, fosnot, fosnaught, fausnaught, fassnacht) is a fried doughnut of Pennsylvania Dutch origin served traditionally in the days of Carnival or on Shrove Tuesday, the day before Lent starts. Fasnachts were made as a way to empty the pantry of lard, sugar, fat, and butter, which were traditionally fasted from during Lent. They are commonly associated with Pennsylvania Dutch cuisine, though they are not exclusive to it. They are found in some other areas of the United States with large German-American populations."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-fasnacht-doughnut"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fasnacht_(doughnut)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Cuisine of the Pennsylvania Dutch","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-pennsylvania-dutch"]]},{"h":"More from Cuisine of the Pennsylvania Dutch","links":[["Lebanon bologna","dish/lebanon-bologna"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/d/db/US_supermarket_fasnacht_pastries%2C_rectangular%2C_Feb_2013.jpg/500px-US_supermarket_fasnacht_pastries%2C_rectangular%2C_Feb_2013.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Jim10701","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:US_supermarket_fasnacht_pastries%2C_rectangular%2C_Feb_2013.jpg"}},"ingredient/white-bread":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/white-bread","n":"White bread","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 3 dishes across 3 cuisines","intro":[["White bread typically refers to breads made from wheat flour from which the bran and the germ layers have been removed from the whole wheatberry as part of the flour grinding or milling process, producing a light-colored flour."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-white-bread"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_bread"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["Dutch cuisine","cuisine/dutch-cuisine",[["Uitsmijter","dish/uitsmijter"]]],["Minnesotan cuisine","cuisine/minnesotan-cuisine",[["Hot beef commercial","dish/hot-beef-commercial"]]],["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine",[["Pozharsky cutlet","dish/pozharsky-cutlet"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Gravy","ingredient/gravy"],["Mashed potato","ingredient/mashed-potato"],["Pot roast","ingredient/pot-roast"],["Bread crumbs","ingredient/bread-crumbs"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Veal","ingredient/veal"],["Fried egg","ingredient/fried-egg"],["Gouda","ingredient/gouda"],["Ham","ingredient/ham"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/2/2c/Wei%C3%9Fbrot-1.jpg/500px-Wei%C3%9Fbrot-1.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Rainer Zenz","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wei%C3%9Fbrot-1.jpg"}},"ingredient/sugar-cane-molasses":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sugar-cane-molasses","n":"Sugar cane molasses","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Molasses ( ), also called black treacle, is a viscous byproduct principally obtained from the refining of sugarcane or sugar beet juice into sugar. Molasses varies in the amount of sugar, the method of extraction, and the age of the plant. Sugarcane molasses is usually used to sweeten and flavour foods. Molasses is a major constituent of fine commercial brown sugar."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sugar-cane-molasses"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sugar_cane_molasses"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Brazilian cuisine","cuisine/brazilian-cuisine",[["Manuê","dish/manue"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Corn","ingredient/corn"]]}]},"dish/masala-chai":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/masala-chai","n":"Masala chai","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Masala chai also known as chai latte is a popular beverage originating from India. It is made by adding aromatic herbs and spices to chai, which is itself made from brewing black tea (usually crush, tear, curl) in milk and water, and sweetening with sugar (often using aeration techniques only performed by masters or \"tevanas\")."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-masala-chai"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Masala_chai"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indian cuisine","cuisine/indian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Black tea","ingredient/black-tea"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Swasthi's Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"indianhealthyrecipes.com","note":"Swasthi Shreekanth's long-running blog of everyday Indian home cooking from across the regions.","url":"https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Hari Ghotra","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"harighotra.co.uk","note":"UK-based cook Hari Ghotra's recipe library and videos of home-style Indian dishes.","url":"https://www.harighotra.co.uk/indian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Indian cuisine","links":[["Akuri","dish/akuri"],["Aloo paratha","dish/aloo-paratha"],["Amba (condiment)","dish/amba-condiment"],["Baingan bharta","dish/baingan-bharta"],["Bombay potato","dish/bombay-potato"],["Butter chicken","dish/butter-chicken"],["Chaat masala","dish/chaat-masala"],["Chicken Chettinad","dish/chicken-chettinad"],["Dahi vada","dish/dahi-vada"],["Dal dhokli","dish/dal-dhokli"],["Dal makhani","dish/dal-makhani"],["Fafda","dish/fafda"],["Falooda","dish/falooda"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["Handvo","dish/handvo"],["Hyderabadi haleem","dish/hyderabadi-haleem"],["Idli","dish/idli"],["Indian restaurant","dish/indian-restaurant"],["Kachumber","dish/kachumber"],["Kidyo","dish/kidyo"],["Kulfi","dish/kulfi"],["Mirchi bada","dish/mirchi-bada"],["Mokthuk","dish/mokthuk"],["Naan","dish/naan"],["Osmania biscuit","dish/osmania-biscuit"],["Panipuri","dish/panipuri"],["Pathia","dish/pathia"],["Rabri","dish/rabri"],["Shemai","dish/shemai"],["Tandoori chicken","dish/tandoori-chicken"],["Tandoori roti","dish/tandoori-roti"],["Thali","dish/thali"],["Zarda (food)","dish/zarda-food"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/0/04/Masala_Chai.JPG/500px-Masala_Chai.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Miansari66","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Masala_Chai.JPG"}},"dish/pepes":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pepes","n":"Pepes","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Pepes is an Indonesian cooking method using banana leaves as food wrappings. The banana-leaf package containing food is secured with lidi seumat (a small nail made from the central ribs of coconut leaves) and then steamed or grilled on charcoal. This cooking technique allows the rich spice mixture to be compressed against the main ingredients inside the individual banana-leaf package while being cooked and also adds a distinct aroma of cooked or burned banana leaves. Although being cooked simultaneously with food, the banana leaf is a non-edible material and is discarded after consuming the food."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pepes"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pepes"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Banana leaf","ingredient/banana-leaf"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/2/2d/Pepes_ikan_emas_%28pais_lauk_mas%29_Sunda.jpg/500px-Pepes_ikan_emas_%28pais_lauk_mas%29_Sunda.jpg","w":500,"h":368,"by":"Gunawan Kartapranata","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pepes_ikan_emas_(pais_lauk_mas)_Sunda.jpg"}},"ingredient/salsa-sauce":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/salsa-sauce","n":"Salsa (sauce)","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["A salsa is any of a variety of sauces used as condiments for tacos and other Mexican and Mexican-American foods, and as dips for tortilla chips. They may be raw or cooked, and are generally served at room temperature."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-salsa-sauce"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salsa_(sauce)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",[["Quesadilla","dish/quesadilla"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Flour tortilla","ingredient/flour-tortilla"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Tortilla","ingredient/tortilla"]]}]},"ingredient/date":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/date","n":"Date","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Phoenix dactylifera, commonly known as the date palm, is a flowering-plant species in the palm family Arecaceae, native to the region from the Gulf States and Iraq to Pakistan and India. It is cultivated for its edible sweet fruit called dates. The species is widely cultivated across northern Africa, the Middle East, Australia, South and Southeast Asia, the coastal Mediterranean basin, and Southern California. It is naturalised in many tropical and subtropical regions worldwide. P. dactylifera is the type species of genus Phoenix, which contains 12–19 species of wild date palms."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-date"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Date_(fruit)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Turkish cuisine","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",[["Rakı","dish/rak"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Dates","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":9662762,"top":[["Egypt","cuisine/egyptian-cuisine",1745094],["Saudi Arabia","cuisine/saudi-arabian-cuisine",1709798],["Algeria","cuisine/algerian-cuisine",1249000],["Iran","cuisine/iranian-cuisine",1117940],["Iraq","cuisine/iraqi-cuisine",678361],["Pakistan","cuisine/pakistani-cuisine",625293],["Sudan","cuisine/sudanese-cuisine",450759],["Oman","cuisine/omani-cuisine",383072],["Tunisia","cuisine/tunisian-cuisine",366674],["United Arab Emirates","cuisine/emirati-cuisine",354252],["Libya","cuisine/libyan-cuisine",182927],["China","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",162488],["Morocco","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine",130024],["Kuwait","cuisine/kuwaiti-cuisine",106868],["Israel","cuisine/israeli-cuisine",65370]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Barrel","ingredient/barrel"],["Fig","ingredient/fig"],["Grape","ingredient/grape"],["Pomace","ingredient/pomace"]]}]},"dish/tarta-de-santiago":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/tarta-de-santiago","n":"Tarta de Santiago","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Galician cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Torta de Santiago (in Galician) or Tarta de Santiago (in Spanish), literally meaning cake of St. James, is an almond cake or pie from Galicia with its origin in the Middle Ages and the Camino de Santiago. The ingredients mainly consist of ground almonds (almond flour), eggs, and sugar, with additional flavouring of lemon zest, sweet wine, brandy, or grape marc, depending on the recipe used. It is the most well known of the cakes of Galicia."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-tarta-de-santiago"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarta_de_Santiago"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Galician cuisine","cuisine/galician-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":9,"links":[["Almond","ingredient/almond"],["Almond meal","ingredient/almond-meal"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Cinnamomum verum","ingredient/cinnamomum-verum"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Powdered sugar","ingredient/powdered-sugar"],["Sherry","ingredient/sherry"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"More from Galician cuisine","links":[["Androlla","dish/androlla"],["Caldo galego","dish/caldo-galego"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Lacón","dish/lacon"],["Polbo á feira","dish/polbo-a-feira"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/c/ce/Tarta_de_Santiago-2009.jpg/500px-Tarta_de_Santiago-2009.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Tamorlan","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tarta_de_Santiago-2009.jpg"}},"ingredient/leaf":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/leaf","n":"Leaf","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["A leaf is a principal appendage of the stem of a vascular plant, usually borne laterally above ground and specialized for photosynthesis. Leaves are collectively called foliage, as in \"autumn foliage\", while the leaves, stem, flower, and fruit collectively form the shoot system. In most leaves, the primary photosynthetic tissue is the palisade mesophyll and is located on the upper side of the blade or lamina of the leaf, but in some species, including the mature foliage of Eucalyptus, palisade mesophyll is present on both sides and the leaves are said to be isobilateral. The leaf is an integral part of the stem system, and most leaves are flattened and have distinct upper (adaxial) and lower (abaxial) surfaces that differ in color, hairiness, the number of stomata (pores that intake and output gases), the amount and structure of epicuticular wax, and other features. Leaves"]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-leaf"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leaf"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Ulam (salad)","dish/ulam-salad"]]],["Malay cuisine","cuisine/malay-cuisine",[["Ulam (salad)","dish/ulam-salad"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Vegetables","ingredient/vegetables"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/c/c7/Lisc_lipy.jpg/500px-Lisc_lipy.jpg","w":500,"h":592,"by":"Krzysztof P. Jasiutowicz","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lisc_lipy.jpg"}},"ingredient/rib-chop":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/rib-chop","n":"Rib chop","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["A rib chop, or rib end cut, is a cut of meat that comes from the rib section of an animal. The term is usually used for pork and lamb. Rib chops are considered the ribeye of pork and lamb."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-rib-chop"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rib_chop"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine",[["Veal Milanese","dish/veal-milanese"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Sirloin","ingredient/sirloin"]]}],"img":{"src":"/world-cuisine/img/thumb/b/b7/Grilled_Elk_rib_chops-01.jpg/500px-Grilled_Elk_rib_chops-01.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Neeta Lind","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grilled_Elk_rib_chops-01.jpg"}},"ingredie